  "parentCard": {
    "title": "The kitchen pattern parade",
    "minutes": 15,
    "includes": "sing",
    "steps": [
      "Line up behind each other and march a two and two pattern down the hallway, singing it as you go: clap, clap, stomp, stomp, clap, clap, stomp, stomp.",
      "Now a four in a row parade: clap, stomp, spin, tap. Sing the four words in order and march them twice around the kitchen.",
      "Make them the parade leader. They invent the pattern, you follow behind and copy it exactly, mistakes and all.",
      "Make your last pattern one beat longer than any of theirs, and see if they can march it back to you."
    ],
    "notice": [
      "When the parade speeds up, do they keep the pairs together, or do the two and two slide apart?",
      "When they lead, do they invent a pattern longer than two beats without being asked?"
    ]
  }
